# Next.js + TypeScript

- Use App Router (`app/`). Prefer Server Components by default; add `"use client"` only when needed (state, effects, browser APIs, event handlers).
- Colocate route UI under `app/`; shared UI under `components/`; API/clients under `lib/` or `services/`.
- Name components in PascalCase; hooks as `useX`; utilities as camelCase.
- Prefer named exports for reusable components/hooks; default export only for Next.js route/page files when required.
- Fetch data on the server when possible. For client fetching, handle loading/error/empty states explicitly.
- Do not put secrets in client code. Use `NEXT_PUBLIC_` only for safe public config.
- Build UI with Material 3 (MUI). Style via theme tokens (`sx`, `styled`, theme palette/typography/shape); avoid ad-hoc CSS/Tailwind for core components.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — unnecessary client boundary
"use client";
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await getData();
  return <List items={data} />;
}

// ✅ GOOD — server by default
export default async function Page() {
  const data = await getData();
  return <List items={data} />;
}
```
